    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense regarding the protonation. If I replace or supplement the lecithin with a modified starch or a gum like xanthan to build more viscosity, how much of a difference does that actually make in preventing the oil from breaking out? I'm trying to see if I can compensate for that loss in electrostatic repulsion just by increasing the continuous phase viscosity.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
