      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increasing continuous phase viscosity significantly slows oil droplet movement and Ostwald ripening, which can mechanically delay but not fully eliminate coalescence in low-acid emulsions. For a low-fat mayonnaise, gums like xanthan are generally more effective than modified starches for enhancing integral stability because they improve water retention rather than just gel strength. Ultimately, while viscosity helps, replacing lecithin entirely in this highly acidic environment will likely fail because the critical mechanism of interfacial charge repulsion is lost.",
